`aplan verify` opens the repository (unlike hermetic `check`). Its resolution
behaviour, APLAN011/012/015 against real commits, is covered exhaustively by
the git-backed corpus in `crates/aplan-e2e`; here we pin the CLI contract.

A bad `--format` is rejected before anything else, so it needs no repository:

```
$ aplan verify --format bogus
? 2
aplan: unknown format `bogus` (expected human, json, agent, github)

```
